    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by two high-upside plays against favorable arms. **Miguel Vargas** leads our output with a 63.96 score; he faces Andrew Abbott, whose high xERA (5.02) provides an excellent foundation for a strong offensive day. **Vargas** benefits from a substantial 19% boost due to the favorable SP matchup and a clean #3 spot in the order. Similarly, **Kyle Tucker** (60.91) remains an essential start despite a neutral platoon disadvantage against Shane Drohan. While **Tucker** loses a point for the platoon dynamic, his elite base projection and the high probability of run production from the #4 spot ensure he remains a cornerstone of our daily offensive strategy. \n\nStrategic considerations for today revolve heavily around speed and matchup exploitation. **Nasim Nunez** (50.00) is locked into the utility role primarily due to his high-efficiency profile against Kevin Gausman; he receives a 4% bonus for Gausman\u2019s slow delivery, which significantly increases his stolen base upside\u2014a critical differentiator in our roster construction. **Wade Meckler** (38.70) was the closest exclusion from the starting lineup, ultimately benched because the optimizer prioritized the higher floor of our current outfield mix against the formidable presence of Jacob deGrom. The primary risk across the board remains the \"Lineup Pending\" status for all starters; should defensive shifts or last-minute rest days alter the projected batting order, the efficiency scores for **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, and **Heliot Ramos** will require recalibration. We are also monitoring the availability of **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jackson Merrill**, who are off today, and continuing to track **Jordan Westburg** as he remains sidelined on the IL.",
